    "feature": "Regulate and validate top-level JSON arrays in request items. A request item like `:=[1,2,3]` should produce a top-level JSON array under the empty key, represented by a dedicated regulated array type (not a plain list that can be mis-cast). Mixing a top-level array with conflicting access at the same level (for example a top-level array followed by an append `[]:=`, or an append followed by a top-level array) must raise a clear HTTPie type/syntax error rather than silently overwriting."
